Shorthands in object creation:

- Not a new keyword, but it can also catch your attention when reading ES2015 code. There is now a
    shortcut for creating objects.
- when the object property you want to create has the same name as the variable used as the value.

            function createPony() {
                const name = 'Rainbow Dash';        // variable
                const color = 'blue';
                return { name: name, color: color }; // return object(object property has the same name as variable)
            }
    
    can be simplified to:

            function createPony() {
                const name = 'Rainbow Dash';
                const color = 'blue';
                return { name, color };
            }

- Similarly, when you want to define a method in the object:

            function createPony() {
                return {                            // return object
                    run: () => {                    // method
                        console.log('Run!');
                    }
                };
            }
    
    can be simplified to:

            function createPony() {
                return {
                    run() {
                        console.log('Run!');
                    }
                };
            }
